From aecb4d530b0034cc820f41124a05880a43721de1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:38:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: lay out multi-column containers in columns

column-count and column-width were parsed (NavGator enables
layout.columns.enabled) but layout ignored them, so a multicol list
rendered as one full-width column. Dailymotion's Explore feed is a
column-count: 4 list of break-inside: avoid cards and drew each card at
the width of the whole feed.

Layout has no block fragmentation, so the content is laid out once at
the used column width (css-multicol's pseudo-algorithm) and its
top-level boxes are then distributed over the columns at the shortest
balanced height, truncating margins at column breaks. Boxes are never
split, which matches the masonry pattern exactly. Text directly inside
the container would need line-level fragmentation and keeps the old
full-width layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
